# C++ Basics
Ok so I made 5 programs which they are named on what I want to focused on which are Loops, Functions, Conditional, Classes, and Data Structure. There is Hello World but that's just a small practice round to understand how I'm going to code and how I'm going to run the programs.

## Instructions for Build and Use

Steps to build and/or run the software:

1. So to even use C++ download C/C++ from microsoft in the extensions tab in Visual Studio Code
2. Make sure that you navigate to the folder where the program you want to run is in
3. To run a program you need to compile to turn the code executable which to do put in terminal: g++ filename.cpp -o filename
4. After it's compiled and if done correctly you should see that a new file was added
5. When it's compiled run the program in terminal to see if it works which you put this in terminal: ./filename

